@startuml
title SYS01 - Recovery to a previously working release

actor Operator
participant "Deployment workflow (deploy.yml)" as Workflow
database "Runner PostgreSQL 18\n(ephemeral / isolated)" as RunnerDB
participant "Requested retained API image" as OldAPI
participant "GitHub artifacts" as Artifacts
participant "VM release manifest" as Metadata
participant "DEI VM deploy script" as Deploy
participant "Versioned runtime configuration" as Config
participant "Nginx" as Nginx
database "Shared DEI PostgreSQL 18" as DEIDB

Operator -> Workflow: Dispatch rollback with release SHA
Workflow -> Workflow: Wait in shared `dei-release` queue
Workflow -> Workflow: Acquire queue slot; validate operation and SHA
Workflow -> Metadata: Read release image IDs, config and current migration version
Metadata --> Workflow: Return requested release and active schema metadata
Workflow -> RunnerDB: Create scratch DB at active schema version
Workflow -> OldAPI: Run compatibility suite against current schema version

alt Requested version is incompatible or release is unretained
  OldAPI --> Workflow: Compatibility/manifest check fails
  Workflow -> Artifacts: Archive sanitized rejection evidence
  Workflow --> Operator: Reject before SSH; VM remains unchanged
else Compatibility passes
  OldAPI --> Workflow: Prior-version reads/writes pass on scratch DB
  Workflow -> Deploy: Verify SSH host key; restore retained release
  Deploy -> Metadata: Recheck manifest and active schema version under VM lock
  Metadata --> Deploy: Release remains eligible
  Deploy -> Config: Select configuration revision paired with release
  Config --> Deploy: Provide selected configuration
  Deploy -> Nginx: Activate requested images and routing
  OldAPI -> DEIDB: Previous API connects to shared database
  DEIDB --> OldAPI: Connection succeeds
  Nginx --> Deploy: HTTPS, API and SPA smoke checks pass
  Deploy -> Metadata: Record restored active SHA and recovery run ID
  Deploy --> Workflow: Recovery verified
  Workflow -> Artifacts: Archive sanitized recovery logs and manifest
  Workflow --> Operator: Rollback successful; release queue slot released
end

note over Workflow,DEIDB
  Rollback does not rebuild images or modify/restore the shared database.
  The requested version must pass compatibility against the current schema
  in an isolated scratch database before the VM is changed. The concurrency
  slot remains held through verification, activation and archival.
end note
@enduml
